From ef254fb1216d75599f06316bf0540f873e868386 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 07:32:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06848/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): ka59 L5 -> L6 (+1), sk48
 honest null

Continuation of round-3. ka59 solved the "isolated chamber" mystery left
open in round 2: the lower cycling stack transport is not a fixed
one-way trap, it is itself ballistic -- launching it left twice
relocates the elevator and opens a route to the sealed plus chamber
(solved via the existing backtrack-clamped flight-physics rules);
launching it right twice afterward restores the original route. L7 was
explored (block-aspect-ratio generalization of the transport) but not
solved.

Independently re-verified per project discipline: 5x fresh env.reset() +
replay via the fixed resolver, all 5 confirmed reached_level=6.

sk48: honest null again on L3, but found a new mechanic -- a
brown-headed vertically-connected chain exhibits physical coupling
(touching it at one segment couples the whole chain, so a downward move
drags the entire chain down one lattice row).

reproducible_total_levels: 141 -> 142 (verified against a fresh sum).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
